The repo-vul is at commit d443c0a7b. The description says the vulnerability is a heap-buffer-overflow READ of 9 bytes in fuzz_parse. The HEAD commit d443c0a7b is "fixed potential crash parsing broken latm streams". 

Given the fix is present in the working tree, maybe the actual vulnerability is a DIFFERENT bug that's still present. But the description specifically mentions the LATM-related fix commit as the HEAD.

